004.steps:
1. Device - Log - Settings, set Logging level to Inform, click edit, set Display Events in Log Monitor to 0 seconds, accept;
2. Device - Log - Settings - Network - DNS Security, enable all the DNS Filtering entries, accept; 
3. Rules and Policies - DNS Rules, enable a DNS Policy : Action-Filter, Interface-X0, Profile-Default Profile;
4. DNS - DNS Proxy, enable DNS Proxy cache and clear all the DNS Proxy cache;
5. PC connects to X0, set dns server as X0 IP, do dig www.ea.com;
6. Moniter - Logs - System log, check the logs;
7. Profile Objects - DNS Filtering, set the action of Gaming in Default Profile to Block; 
8. From PC,  do dig www.ea.com again, check the logs.

019.steps:
1. Add a valid profile named "test";
2. Enable a DNS Policy with Action "Filter";
3. Choose "test" profile on Policy Profile;
4. From CLI, enter configure mode;
5. Input:
#dns-security
#dns-filtering
#no profile test
#commit

014.steps:
1.Object - Profile Objects - DNS Filtering;
2. Add some valid profiles;
3. Edit some profiles, change the names and actions;
4. Delete some profiles or delete all;
5. Navigate to System - Diagnostics - Tech Support Report, export TSR;
6. In TSR, check the DNS Filtering Profile Object..
